Temporary upstream workaround: Open WebUI extracts and embeds chat uploads
before a Pipe or Filter runs, and has no setting that keeps them raw for an
external Files API.

https://github.com/open-webui/open-webui/issues/12228 (closed after Filters
gained raw-file access; uploads are still processed)
https://github.com/open-webui/open-webui/pull/27627 (closed unmerged)

ENABLE_FILE_UPLOAD_PROCESSING=false makes POST /api/v1/files store uploads
without processing, as if each request sent process=false. Leaving it unset,
or any other value, keeps upstream behavior. Open WebUI's internal uploads,
such as generated images, keep their own processing choice.

Removal check: an Open WebUI release that can keep chat uploads raw without
this patch.
--- a/open_webui/routers/files.py
+++ b/open_webui/routers/files.py
@@ -292,7 +292,7 @@
         request,
         file=file,
         metadata=metadata,
-        process=process,
+        process=process and os.environ.get('ENABLE_FILE_UPLOAD_PROCESSING', 'true').lower() == 'true',
         process_in_background=process_in_background,
         user=user,
         background_tasks=background_tasks,
